{"id":"chatcmpl-848e40250e0558fc","object":"chat.completion","created":1788642986,"model":"qwen38flashnext","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n  c.id,\n  c.name,\n  SUM(o.amount) AS total_order_value\nFROM customers c\nJOIN orders o\n  ON o.customer_id = c.id\nGROUP BY\n  c.id,\n  c.name\nORDER BY\n  total_order_value DESC\nLIMIT 3;\n```\n\nFor SQL Server, replace `LIMIT 3` with:\n\n```sql\nSELECT TOP 3 ...\nORDER BY total_order_value DESC;\n```","refusal":null,"annotations":null,"audio":null,"function_call":null,"reasoning":"We need answer user's request: \"Write a SQL query that returns the top 3 customers by total order value from tables customers(id,name) and orders(id,customer_id,amount).\"\n\nNeed provide SQL query. Simple. Could include standard ANSI using LIMIT for PostgreSQL/MySQL, or TOP for SQL Server. Need maybe mention portability. Need final concise. Need ensure query returns top 3 customers by total order value. Query:\n\nSELECT c.id, c.name, SUM(o.amount) AS total_order_value\nFROM customers c\nJOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id\nGROUP BY c.id, c.name\nORDER BY total_order_value DESC\nLIMIT 3;\n\nCould include WITH RANK/ROW_NUMBER to handle ties? \"top 3\" usually limit 3. Maybe if ties desired: use rank <=3. But simple answer enough. Could mention if SQL Server: SELECT TOP 3. Need maybe no final analysis.\n"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","stop_reason":null,"token_ids":null,"routed_experts":null}],"service_tier":null,"system_fingerprint":"vllm-0.28.1rc1.dev446+g798544433-tp4-ep-72ccc4a5","usage":{"prompt_tokens":82,"total_tokens":381,"completion_tokens":299,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":195}},"prompt_logprobs":null,"prompt_token_ids":null,"prompt_text":null,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"metrics":null}